      "richText": [
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "Log in using "
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": true,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "ssh -p 2220 bandit4@bandit.labs.overthewire.org"
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": " and the password obtained in the last level. We navigate to the "
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": true,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "inhere"
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": " directory and list its contents, which reveals ten files ("
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": true,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "-file00"
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": " through "
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": true,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "-file09"
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "). We use the Linux wildcard ("
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": true,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "*"
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": ") to "
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": true,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": "cat"
        },
        {
          "bold": false,
          "code": false,
          "href": null,
          "italic": false,
          "plainText": " through all of them in a single command and read down the output for the one chunk that is actual text rather than binary noise, that chunk is "
